Add a filter box to the Merge record list.

With a long merge file it is hard to find the record(s) to print: the Merge
tab only offers a scrolling list of checkboxes plus Select all / Unselect all.

This adds, above the records table:

  * a "Filter records..." box.  Every whitespace-separated word must appear
    (case-insensitively, as plain text) in at least one column of a record
    for it to be shown, so "smith paris" narrows to Smiths in Paris.
  * a counter: "N of M selected", or "N of M shown, K selected" while a
    filter is active.  All records start out selected and hidden records stay
    selected, so without it a user could filter to one record, print, and get
    every record.
  * "Select shown" / "Unselect shown" buttons that change only the records
    currently visible.  The existing Select all / Unselect all still act on
    every record.

Records hidden by the filter keep their checked state and are still printed
if they are checked.  Rows keep their original record numbers, ticking a box
in a filtered list selects the right underlying record, and the filter text
survives Reload and a change of merge source.

Implementation notes:
  * MergeView puts a QSortFilterProxyModel subclass between MergeTableModel
    and the QTableView.  This also stops leaking a MergeTableModel on every
    reload (they previously had no parent and were never deleted).
  * merge::Merge gains setSelectedRecords(rows, state), which emits
    selectionChanged() once.  Looping over setSelected() would refresh the
    whole table once per row.  Covered by a new case in TestMerge.
  * No change to the file format, to printing, or to any other dialog.

glabels_C.ts is deliberately not touched; new strings show untranslated
(English) until the maintainer next runs lupdate.

Removable if upstream adds an equivalent filter to the Merge tab.

